(Nadиge DURAND FILORGA  2-4 Rue de Lisbonne 75008 , Paris, France  STUDY DESIGN  Study Objectives:   Clinical scoring : Firmness measurement and lifting effect of a Lift GF cream, Instrumental :Firmness measurement and lifting effect of a Lift GF cream, Preliminary Report et Pre Screening  Mйthodologie:   Assessment of firming and lifting efficacy: twice-daily application \(morning and evening\) to the entire face and neck.  Number of Panelists:   30  Inclusion Criteria:   Pre-Recruitment & Screening Visit: Hydration level between 25 and 50 UA corneometer , R0 values at baseline between 0,30 to 0,60mm and 50% sensitive skin; 30 Female aged 40-60 years old; With a lack of firmness / sagging of the face; Skin Fitzpatrick Phototype I to VI  Exclusion Criteria:   Pregnancy and Breastfeeding: Pregnant or breastfeeding women. Surgical History: Face or neck lift \(cervico-facial lift\) within the past 5 years. Aesthetic Medicine: No Dermal filler injections or mesotherapy sessions within the past 12 months.  Skin Types \(Phototypes\):   I, II, III, IV, V, VI  Description   Unit   Unit Price Excl. VAT Total Price Excl. VAT VAT  OBJECTIVE : CLINICAL SCORING : FIRMNESS MEASUREMENT AND LIFTING EFFECT OF A LIFT GF CREAM  Measurement Time/Duration: T0, T7, T28, T56, T84  Lower Face Sagging \(Bazin Scale\) Clinical grading on a scale from 0 \(none\) to 5 \(severe\)   150   15 А   2 250 А   20%  Global Lifting Aspect Expert assessment of the tightening effect on a scale from 0 \(no effect\) to 10 \(maximal lifting effect\)   150   15 А   2 250 А   20%) Tj
